STEP 9 — VISUAL CHECK  (run; headless browser was already installed)
  2 captures taken (landing, demo), 1 re-capture after edits. Within cap.
  demo.html: clean on first look. Status band, tabs, four balance plates with
    rosette corners, ledger with filter chips and cinnabar declined rows all
    render as intended. No overlap, no off-canvas elements, contrast fine.
    No edits needed.
  index.html: real finding. Everything below the hero rendered at opacity 0.
    Cause: .reveal starts hidden and is only unhidden by IntersectionObserver,
    so any context where the observer does not fire leaves content invisible
    while still occupying layout height. Scrolling users were always fine, but
    the content was one failed observer away from a blank page.
    Fixed in three parts:
      1. Scoped the hiding rules to .js .reveal, so with JS off or blocked the
         page renders fully visible instead of blank.
      2. Added a small head script that only adds the .js class when
         IntersectionObserver exists and reduced-motion is not requested, so
         the page opts into the animation only when it can complete it.
      3. Added a load + 1.5s fallback that reveals everything unconditionally.
    The full-page screenshot still shows the fold-and-below blank, because
    Playwright captures without scrolling and the observer legitimately never
    fires. That is a capture artifact, not a page defect. The three changes
    above mean no real visitor can end up on invisible content.
  Re-validated after the edits: scripts/validate-entry.sh -> OK (exit 0).

